---
source: tests/help.rs
expression: help(&path)
---
Create a sandbox if needed and attach to its agent

Usage: bento run [OPTIONS] [TARGETS]... [-- <AGENT_ARGS>...]

Arguments:
  [TARGETS]...
          Agent or workload kit (registry reference or local path, e.g. ./kit), then workspace paths (default: the current directory)

  [AGENT_ARGS]...
          Arguments for the agent

Options:
  -D, --debug
          Enable debug logging: each smolvm call, and SMOLBENTO_LOG at info unless set

      --name <NAME>
          Sandbox name (default: <agent>-<workspace basename>)

      --cpus <CPUS>
          Number of CPUs (0 = all host CPUs)

      --no-input
          Never prompt; commands that need an answer fail with the command to run instead

  -m, --memory <MEMORY>
          Memory, e.g. 4g (default: half of host memory, 512MiB to 32GiB)

  -e, --env <ENV>
          Environment variable: KEY=VALUE, or KEY to copy the host's value

      --env-file <ENV_FILE>
          Read environment variables from a file

  -p, --publish <PUBLISH>
          Publish a port: [[IP:]HOST:]PORT[/proto]

  -t, --template <TEMPLATE>
          Image to use instead of the agent's template

      --pull <PULL>
          Kit pull policy: always, missing, or never with a saved template [default: a cached kit's tag is checked again once a day]

      --clone
          Work on a private clone of the git repo; its commits come back via the sandbox-<name> git remote

      --kit <REF>
          Add a kit: registry reference or local path, e.g. ./kit (repeatable)

      --kit-arg <NAME=VALUE>
          Kit argument: NAME=VALUE, or KIT.NAME=VALUE for one kit (repeatable)

      --kit-args-file <FILE>
          Read kit arguments (NAME=VALUE lines) from a file (repeatable)

      --mount <HOST:SANDBOX_PATH>
          Bind a host directory to a kit host-mount@1 path (can be repeated): HOST:SANDBOX_PATH. Can only be used when creating a new sandbox

      --deny-network <HOST>
          Add a per-sandbox network deny rule at creation time. Can be specified multiple times. The rule applies only to the new sandbox and can be listed or removed later with 'bento policy ls <NAME>' or 'bento policy rm network --sandbox <NAME> --resource <HOST>'

      --skills <SKILLS>
          Shared skills: off, readonly (store linked in read-only) or readwrite (store mounted over the agent's skills directory). Default: skills.defaultMode

      --static-mcp <SERVERS>
          Registered MCP servers for the agent, comma-separated (see `bento mcp`), or `none`

  -d, --detach
          Start the sandbox and leave it running

      --rm
          Remove the sandbox when the agent exits

      --no-progress
          Suppress progress output

  -w, --workdir <WORKDIR>
          Directory to start the agent session in: absolute, or relative to the sandbox workspace. Applies to this session only, so it works on a re-attach too

  -h, --help
          Print help

Examples:
  bento run claude
  bento run claude ~/code/api
  bento run codex . -- --model o3
